.com/fkt-podcast</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/fkt-podcast/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[The podcast of fastestknowntime.com. Learn about the best FKT routes, who did them, and how fast.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">EvokeCast</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/evokecast/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="EvokeCast" /><published>2026-06-04T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-06-04T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/evokecast</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/evokecast/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="science" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Join Scott Johnston and the Evoke Endurance coaching team for regular interviews, discussion, and educational materials for the global mountain community.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Historias del Trail</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/historias-del-trail/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Historias del Trail" /><published>2026-06-04T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-06-04T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/historias-del-trail</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/historias-del-trail/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="skyrunning" /><category term="subultra" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Spanish podcast with Albert Jorquera - a trail running journalist, commentator, writer, podcast host, and ultrarunner.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Long Run Labs</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/long-run-labs/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Long Run Labs" /><published>2026-06-04T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-06-04T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/long-run-labs</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/long-run-labs/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="business" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Science of Running</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/science-of-running/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Science of Running" /><published>2026-06-04T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-06-04T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/science-of-running</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/science-of-running/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="science" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Author and coach Steve Magness takes an in depth look at training, coaching, sport science, and anything else that relates to enhancing endurance performance.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">The Buzz</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-buzz/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="The Buzz" /><published>2026-06-04T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-06-04T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-buzz</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-buzz/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[A podcast that cuts through the noise of ultra trail running with grounded takes from a true expert in the sport. As a pioneering ultrarunner, FKT legend, and industry veteran, Buzz brings decades of experience and a sharp, critical eye to the big ideas shaping endurance sports.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">The Ultra Sound Podcast</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-ultra-sound-podcast/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="The Ultra Sound Podcast" /><published>2026-06-04T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-06-04T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-ultra-sound-podcast</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/the-ultra-sound-podcast/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="trail" /><category term="ultra" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Pro trailrunner Tom Evans and his best friend Brett Saunders discuss all things trailrunning.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Team Macody Podcast</title><link href="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/team-macody-podcast/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Team Macody Podcast" /><published>2026-06-03T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-06-03T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/team-macody-podcast</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://bestrunningpodcasts.com/team-macody-podcast/"><![CDATA[]]></content><author><name>Hans Kristian Smedsrød Engdahl</name><email>hans@naerdetalvor.no</email></author><category term="podcast" /><category term="road" /><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Norwegian road running podcast. Weekly chats with the Macody brothers + friends recorded with the Clubhouse app. Listening to it feels like you're listening in on a bunch of dudes talking shit in a locker room. So bad it's god. Takes a while to get used to the characters, but once you're in you're in.]]></summary></entry></feed>